<h2>Setting Up the Putnen Under Desk Elliptical</h2>
<p>Compact seated ellipticals usually arrive mostly assembled, so you can be pedaling within minutes. A little care with placement makes daily use far more comfortable.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check the fittings.</strong> Make sure the pedals and crank arms are tight before your first session, since shipping can loosen them.</li>
<li><strong>Power the monitor.</strong> If the display runs on a battery, fit it and confirm it wakes when you start pedaling.</li>
<li><strong>Pick a flat spot.</strong> A hard floor with a rubber mat works best. Deep carpet can make the base rock.</li>
<li><strong>Set your distance.</strong> Sit in your usual chair and slide the machine until your knees stay slightly bent at full extension and clear the desk at the top of the stride.</li>
<li><strong>Start at the lowest resistance</strong> and raise it only once pedaling feels automatic while you work.</li>
